# The Python packages needed to build the documentation, for pip-compile.
#
# This file lists only the packages the documentation uses itself, i.e.,
# Sphinx and the theme and extensions that doc/conf.py loads, with loose
# version limits.  requirements.txt, next to it, is generated from it
# by pip-compile (from the pip-tools package) and pins every package needed,
# including the dependencies of these, to an exact version.  Read the Docs
# (as set in .readthedocs.yaml in the top-level directory of the repo) and
# the vx_docs conda environment install requirements.txt, so that every
# build uses the same versions.
#
# Edit this file, not requirements.txt.  After editing it, regenerate
# requirements.txt from the doc directory with:
#
#   pip-compile requirements.in
#
sphinx~=8.0.0
sphinx_rtd_theme>=3.0.0
sphinxcontrib-bibtex>=2.6.4
sphinxcontrib-plantuml
setuptools<81.0.0
